ered event timestamps tying 1885 to 1460 through a succession of interactions within 600 time units, the temporal evidence is insufficient to conclude a genuine time-respecting cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_82bdb271\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460],\n  \"window\": [8483, 37283],\n  \"confidence\": 0.25,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"There are no direct events between 1885 and 1460 in the window (step_04) and both nodes have very few events overall in the interval (1885:5, 1460:4; step_06), so the temporal evidence for a time-respecting chain is weak. Static k-hop views show many possible static neighbors (steps_02 and _03) and overall activity in the window is substantial (step_01) with other highly active nodes present (step_05); these are potential confounders if one ignored timing. Given the absence of temporally ordered event timestamps tying 1885 to 1460 through a succession of interactions within 600 time units, the temporal evidence is insufficient to conclude a genuine time-respecting cascade.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 29414, "total_output_tokens": 4898, "total_tokens": 34312, "total_latency_ms": 56586, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}